    "q-108458": {
      "dom_id": "step-q108458",
      "name": "Question 5",
      "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14265567/assets/0c1aa4aba4a5d8ea2a00bbb5e94bcc61764ed97a6bf8b434138310d45f7cd35d.png)\n\nThe speed-time graph represents the motion of a $250\\text{cc}$ motorcycle at the start of a race. Calculate the acceleration of the motorcycle.",
      "worked_solution": "In a speed-time graph, the acceleration is given by the slope of the line.\n\nThe line passes through the points $(0,0)$ and $(8,28),$ so its slope is:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m & =\\frac{28\\,\\text{m/s}-0\\,\\text{m/s}}{8\\,\\text{s}-0\\,\\text{s}} \\\\  & =\\frac{28\\,\\text{m/s}}{8\\,\\text{s}} \\\\  & =3.5\\,\\frac{\\text{m}}{{\\text{s}}^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the acceleration of the $250\\text{cc}$ motorcycle is $3.5\\,{\\text{m/s}}^{2}.$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
